ag can parse and reserialize unrelated Dags in the same bundle, adding work each time a developer tests or debugs a Dag. This change limits parsing to the owning source file when the stored file location points to a regular file inside that bundle.\n\nFor a bundle containing `orders.py` and `reports.py`, testing a Dag in `orders.py` previously parsed the whole bundle. It now parses `orders.py`, including sibling Dags defined in that file so same-file `TriggerDagRunOperator` targets remain available. Packaged or unavailable source files still use the complete bundle.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The regression asserts that `DAG.test()` passes the parent source file to `BundleDagBag` rather than the whole bundle.\n- Earlier validation recorded in this PR: 10 focused Dag.test tests passed in Breeze, with Ruff lint and formatting checks and `git diff --check` passing.\n- Hosted checks on head `5fc4379d3076b6bcf0b971a9a8491c6656631474`: 68 successful, 38 skipped, and CodeQL neutral; no failed or pending checks.\n- This maintenance pass did not rerun local tests or reproduce the reported VSCode debugging session. The added assertion covers the regular-file path; it does not independently test every packaged-file fallback.\n\nFixes #72513\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes (OpenAI Codex (GPT-6))\n\nGenerated-by: OpenAI Codex (GPT-6) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\n---\n\n* Read the **[Pull Request Guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#pull-request-guidelines)** for more information. Note: commit author/co-author name and email in commits become permanently public when merged.\n* For fundamental code changes, an Airflow Improvement Proposal ([AIP](https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/AIRFLOW/Airflow+Improvement+Proposals)) is needed.\n* When adding dependency, check compliance with the [ASF 3rd Party License Policy](https://www.apache.org/legal/resolved.html#category-x).\n* For significant user-facing changes create newsfragment: `{pr_number}.significant.rst`, in [airflow-core/newsfragments](https://github.com/apache/airflow/tree/main/airflow-core/newsfragments). You can add this file in a follow-up commit after the PR is created so you know the PR number.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/72658/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]
